The outgoing flight change to May 16th and return to May 14th creates an impossible itinerary because the return flight would occur before the departure. This is not feasible. I must inform the user of this error and request clarification on the dates. 

Action:
{"name": "transfer_to_human_agents", "arguments": {"summary": "User requests to delay outgoing flight by one day and move return flight back by one day for reservation HXDUBJ, but this creates a return date before departure (May 14th before May 16th). The itinerary is impossible. User needs to clarify the date adjustments."}}

The reservation XEHM4B has basic economy flights, so it needs to be upgraded to economy before cancellation. The reservation 59XX6W is already in economy and has travel insurance. I will proceed with upgrading reservation XEHM4B to economy. 

Action: 
{"name": "update_reservation_flights", "arguments": {"reservation_id": "XEHM4B", "cabin": "economy", "flights": [{"flight_number": "HAT005", "date": "2024-05-20"}, {"flight_number": "HAT178", "date": "2024-05-30"}], "payment_id": "credit_card_2408938"}}

I apologize for the error. The cabin class must be explicitly specified in the update. Since the original reservation was in basic economy and we are keeping the same cabin, I will include "cabin": "basic_economy" in the update request.  

Action:  
